# This file is automatically read by devenv.sh whenever it is found in the
# current directory. Reading happens early on so you can still override through
# command-line options. devenv.sh will actually look for files named .devenv.env
# and devenv.env (see DEVENV_ENVFILES) in the following directories (see
# DEVENV_PATH). All files found are read, in order, so later files override
# earlier ones. Variables already set in the environment take precedence over
# all files. DEVENV_PATH and DEVENV_ENVFILES cannot be set from these files.
# - /etc
# - /usr/local/etc
# - $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
# - $HOME
# - $(pwd)

# This file is NOT sourced: it only contains KEY=VALUE lines, and values are
# taken literally, i.e. $VAR, $(cmd) or `cmd` are not expanded. Values can be
# enclosed in single or double quotes. Blank lines and lines starting with # are
# ignored, as is anything after a whitespace-preceded # in unquoted values.
#
# Set any variable recognized by devenv.sh, i.e. variables starting with
# DEVENV_. You can also set all variables supported by the tunnel.sh entrypoint,
# as these will be automatically passed to the container when it is created.
# These variables start with TUNNEL_. All other variables are ignored.

# DEVENV_VERBOSE=3
# DEVENV_GITHUB_TOKEN=-  # Do not pass the token of the gh CLI
# TUNNEL_VERBOSE=3
